## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to design a scalable, governed, multi-region data lake with reliable ingestion, deduplication, and schema evolution.

## Key Concepts

- Regional ingestion paths and Parquet data lake
- Lake Formation governance and CRR
- Idempotent ingestion with event_id dedup
- Schema evolution via Avro + Glue Schema Registry
- Late data handling and e2e testing

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode dedupe
async function isDuplicate(event_id){
  const exists = await dynamo.get({PK: event_id});
  if (exists) return true;
  await dynamo.put({PK: event_id, ...});
  return false;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you scale CRR for thousands of regions?
- How would you monitor data quality drift in this setup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical, beginner-friendly understanding of end-to-end data ingestion with a realistic cost-sensitive constraint. It also introduces basic data quality and idempotency patterns not covered in prior questions.

## Key Concepts
- Ingestion pipelines with Glue Studio
- Parquet writing and date partitioning
- Idempotent loads via load_id/marker files
- Basic data quality checks (row count stability, distinct count)
- Cost monitoring with CloudWatch and Budgets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-idempotent marker example (conceptual)
const markerPath = `s3://corp-logs/markers/logs_${yyyymmdd}.marker`;
if (!exists(markerPath)) {
  // run load, then write marker
  mark(markerPath);
}
```

